          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If someone has a raised blood pressure reading but no diagnosis of hypertension, which chapter does that belong in?",
          "answer": "A raised blood pressure reading in someone who has not been diagnosed with hypertension is classified under **ICD-10 Chapter 18**, which deals with symptoms, signs, and abnormal findings (R00-R99). Specifically, it is documented as an abnormal finding rather than a disease. Chapter 9 (diseases of the circulatory system) does not apply in this case until a formal diagnosis of hypertension is made. \n\nYou may want to discuss with a healthcare professional if there are concerns about blood pressure readings or related symptoms, as they can provide tailored advice based on individual health circumstances. \n\nI could not cover any specific diagnostic criteria or treatment options for hypertension here.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
